From ac5a44d5491c030e510b50cf8b48516516787fe6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 03:47:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 121/256] feat(pypto-x): add torch custom-op bridge for the
 AVX-512 linear kernel (W8J)

J0 established that rebuilding a Core IR graph per call cannot live in an
inference hot path, so J1 delivers the kernel bridge instead:

- pypto.framework.linear_kernel builds one rank-2 matmul CoreProgram per
  (dtype, M, K, N, target) and keeps it in an in-process tier plus a
  cross-process disk sidecar next to the content-addressed AVX-512
  artifact.  A second call builds nothing; a second process loads the
  immutable artifact and re-validates it through Avx512Runtime.load with
  no clang invocation.  Cache key and invalidation rules are explicit
  (target dict + lowering/payload/ABI/format versions + bridge key
  version; stale/tampered sidecars fail validation and are rebuilt).
- pypto.framework.torch_bridge converts torch CPU tensors to runtime
  buffers with documented copy counts (0 for contiguous inputs, 1 for a
  contiguous() materialisation) and ownership (the numpy view keeps the
  torch storage alive).
- pypto.framework.torch_ops registers torch.ops.pypto_x.linear (fail-open
  with counters and once-per-reason warnings), linear_strict (fail-closed),
  pack_weight / linear_prepacked (self-describing uint8 handle; one
  (N, K) -> (K, N) pack per weight revision) and fake/meta impls.
- pypto.framework imports neither torch nor numpy: torch stays optional.

Tests: 64 torch-env tests (f32/bf16 correctness including non-square,
bias, odd tails, non-contiguous inputs; zero-copy accounting; compile and
weight-pack cache identity/disk reuse; fail-open vs fail-closed matrix;
meta fake inference and torch.compile tracing; a runtime ABI round-trip
that launches the compiled artifact with torch-backed numpy handles)
plus 4 torch-free tests in the system-python suite pinning the
optional-dependency boundary.
